stance every six months or  so there are certain cities that are  very very  walkable and have a high density of  impressive things per square mile or  kilometer Paris is one such example it  is by far the most beautiful city I've  ever been in Bar None just walking  around and everything catches your eye  as absolutely spectacular and you can do  it relatively inexpensively surprisingly  enough there are neighborhoods where you  can do that and it doesn't require miles  and miles of walking if your parents  have health issues or fatigue issues and  so on so I'd be another one that I would  put on the list of must visits if you  have the opportunity but the world is  your oyster there are many other options  and I could give you easily another 20  that I'm just as excited about but those  are a few of the highlights and happy  travels  be safe be curious be respectful and  think that will get you a long long way  you

